translated_text:
REGENT OF KATINGAN,

Considering : a. that with the enactment of Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection and Law Number 24 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence, it is deemed necessary to prevent and overcome violence against Women and Children through legal protection for Women and Children victims of violence;

b. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection of Women and Children victims of violence;

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 5 of 2002 concerning the Establishment of Katingan Regency, Seruyan Regency, Sukamara Regency, Lamandau Regency, Gunung Mas Regency, Pulang Pisau Regency, Murung Raya Regency and Barito Timur Regency in Central Kalimantan Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 18, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4180);

3. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);

4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 100, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 17 of 2016 concerning the Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 of 2016 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2016 Number 237, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5946);

5. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

6. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);

7. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning the Formulation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 13 of 2022 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning the Formulation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2022 Number 143, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6801);

8. Law Number 16 of 2011 concerning Legal Aid (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 104, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5246);

9. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times most recently by Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 of 2022 concerning Job Creation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2022 Number 238, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6841);

10. Law Number 12 of 2022 concerning the Criminal Act of Social Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2022 Number 120, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);

11. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation for the Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);

12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2008 concerning the Implementation of Women's Protection;

13. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 3 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Child Protection;

14. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2010 Number 466);

15. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for Handling Child Victims of Violence (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 42);

16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 19 of 2011 concerning Guidelines for the Empowerment of Women Victims of Violence (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 903);

17. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2022 concerning Service Standards for the Protection of Women and Children (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2022 Number 85);

With Mutual Approval

text:
BAB II
ASAS, TUJUAN DAN RUANG LINGKUP PENGATURAN
Pasal 2
Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan, dilaksanakan berdasarkan  asas :
a. penghormatan dan pemenuhan terhadap hak-hak korban;
- 5 -
b. keadilan dan kesetaraan gender;
c. non diskriminasi;
d. kepentingan terbaik bagi korban;
e. kearifan lokal;
f. hak untuk hidup, kelangsungan hidup dan perkembangan anak; g. penghargaan terhadap pendapat korban; dan
h. kepastian hukum.

translated_text:
CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES, OBJECTIVES AND SCOPE OF REGULATION
Article 2
Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence, is implemented based on the principles of:
a. respect and fulfillment of victims' rights;
- 5 -
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination;
d. best interests of victims;
e. local wisdom;
f. right to life, survival and development of children; g. respect for victims' opinions; and
h. legal certainty.

text:
Pasal 4
Ruang lingkup Pengaturan Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak Korban Kekerasan  meliputi:
a. hak korban;
b. kewenangan, kewajiban dan tanggung jawab;
c. kelembagaan;
d. standar pelayanan minimal;
e. rumah perlindungan sosial;
f. pelaporan;
g. pembinaan dan pengawasan;
h. peran serta masyarakat; dan
i. pendanaan.

translated_text:
Article 4
The scope of Regulation on Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence includes:
a. rights of victims;
b. authority, obligations and responsibilities;
c. institutional matters;
d. minimum service standards;
e. social protection houses;
f. reporting;
g. guidance and supervision;
h. community participation; and
i. funding.

text:
BAB III
HAK KORBAN
Pasal 5
Setiap Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan berhak :
a. untuk dihormati harkat dan martabatnya sebagai manusia;
b. untuk mendapatkan perlindungan dari keluarga, masyarakat, Pemerintah Daerah  dan pihak lain baik sementara maupun berdasarkan penetapan perintah  Perlindungan dari Pengadilan;
c. mendapatkan pemulihan pelayanan kesehatan fisik, psikologis maupun  seksual sesuai penderitaan yang dialami oleh korban kekerasan;
d. mendapatkan penanganan secara khusus berkaitan dengan kerahasiaan korban; e. mendapatkan pendampingan oleh pendamping dan bantuan hukum pada  setiap tingkat proses pemeriksaan sesuai dengan ketentuan peraturan  perundang-undangan;
f. mendapatkan pelayanan bimbingan rohani.

translated_text:
CHAPTER III
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 5
Every Woman and Child victim of violence has the right:
a. to have their dignity and worth as a human being respected;
b. to obtain protection from family, community, Regional Government and other parties either temporarily or based on the determination of a Protection order from the Court;
c. to obtain recovery of physical, psychological and sexual health services in accordance with the suffering experienced by victims of violence;
d. to obtain special handling related to the confidentiality of victims;
e. to obtain assistance by companions and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
f. to obtain spiritual guidance services.

text:
BAB IV
KEWENANGAN, KEWAJIBAN DAN TANGGUNG JAWAB
Pasal 7
(1) Pemerintah Daerah berwenang dan bertanggung jawab atas Perlindungan  Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan.
(2) Kewajiban dan tanggung jawab Pemerintah Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud pada  ayat (1) meliputi:
a. menjamin hak perempuan dan anak tanpa diskriminasi sesuai peraturan  perundang-undangan;
b. melaksanakan kebijakan perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak korban  kekerasan berdasarkan peraturan perundang-undangan;
c. menetapkan kebijakan, program dan kegiatan perlindungan Perempuan  dan Anak korban kekerasan;
d. memberikan dukungan sarana dan prasarana pelaksanaan perlindungan  Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan;
e. mengalokasikan anggaran dalam penyelenggaraan perlindungan Perempuan  dan Anak korban kekerasan;
f. membina dan mengawasi penyelenggaraan perlindungan Perempuan dan  Anak korban kekerasan;
g. peningkatan kualitas dan kompetensi SDM yang memberikan pelayanan/  pendampingan bagi korban kekerasan pada perempuan dan anak; h. melakukan keijasama dengan masyarakat dan/atau organisasi  kemasyarakatan dalam penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan sesuai  dengan peraturan perundang-undangan;
i. melakukan tindakan preventive dalam rangka mencegah terjadinya  pelanggaran terhadap hak perempuan dan anak.
(3) Tanggung jawab Pemerintah Daerah dalam upaya perlindungan perempuan dan  anak sebagaimana dimaksud pada Pasal 7 ayat (1) dilaksanakan oleh Perangkat  Daerah sesuai dengan tugas dan fungsinya.

translated_text:
CHAPTER IV
AUTHORITY, OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Article 7
(1) The Regional Government has the authority and responsibility for the Protection of Women and Children victims of violence.
(2) The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in paragraph (1) include:
a. guaranteeing the rights of women and children without discrimination in accordance with laws and regulations;
b. implementing policies for the protection of Women and Children victims of violence based on laws and regulations;
c. establishing policies, programs and activities for the protection of Women and Children victims of violence;
d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of Women and Children victims of violence;
e. allocating budget in the implementation of protection of Women and Children victims of violence;
f. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of Women and Children victims of violence;
g. improving the quality and competence of human resources who provide services/assistance for victims of violence against women and children;
h. cooperating with the community and/or community organizations in the implementation of protection of women in accordance with laws and regulations;
i. taking preventive action in order to prevent violations of the rights of women and children.
(3) The responsibility of the Regional Government in efforts to protect women and children as referred to in Article 7 paragraph (1) shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions.

text:
BAB V
KELEMBAGAAN
Pasal 9
(1) UPTD PPA yang telah terbentuk dapat mewadahi lembaga/unit keija yang  memberikan pelayanan bagi korban kekerasan seperti rumah aman, rumah  perlindungan sosial Anak, rumah perlindungan trauma center, rumah  perlindungan sosial wanita, rumah singgah dan lain-lain kegiatan pelayanan  sesuai Peraturan Perundang-undangan yang berlaku.
(2) Bentuk pelayanan yang dilaksanakan UPTD PPA meliputi :
a. penanganan pengaduan;
b. rehabilitasi kesehatan;
c. rehabilitasi sosial;
d. bantuan hukum;
e. pemulihan/layanan psikologis;
- 7 -
f. mediasi; dan
g. pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial.
(3) Pemberian layanan terpadu sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) dilaksanakan  sesuai dengan SPM.

translated_text:
CHAPTER V
INSTITUTIONAL ARRANGEMENTS
Article 9
(1) The established UPTD PPA can accommodate institutions/work units that provide services for victims of violence such as safe houses, social protection houses for Children, trauma center protection houses, women's social protection houses, shelters and other service activities in accordance with applicable Laws and Regulations.
(2) Forms of services implemented by UPTD PPA include:
a. complaint handling;
b. health rehabilitation;
c. social rehabilitation;
d. legal assistance;
e. recovery/psychological services;
- 7 -
f. mediation; and
g. repatriation and social reintegration.
(3) The provision of integrated services as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be implemented in accordance with SPM.

text:
Pasal 11
(1) SPM sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 9 ayat (3) memiliki indikator kineija meliputi :
a. cakupan Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan yang mendapatkan  penanganan pengaduan oleh petugas terlatih di dalam UPTD PPA; b. cakupan Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan yang mendapatkan  layanan kesehatan oleh tenaga kesehatan terlatih di Puskesmas dan di  Rumah Sakit;
c. cakupan layanan rehabilitasi sosial yang diberikan oleh petugas rehabilitasi sosial terlatih bagi Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan di  dalam UPTD PPA;
d. cakupan layanan bimbingan rohani yang diberikan oleh petugas bimbingan rohani terlatih bagi Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan di  dalam UPTD PPA;
e. cakupan layanan bantuan hukum bagi perempuan dan anak korban  kekerasan;
f. cakupan layanan pemulihan/ layanan psikologis bagi perempuan dan anak  korban kekerasan;
g. cakupan layanan mediasi bagi perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan; h. cakupan layanan pemulangan bagi perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan;  dan
i. cakupan layanan reintegrasi sosial bagi perempuan dan anak korban  kekerasan.
(2) Penetapan indikator kineija SPM UPTD PPA bagi Perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) merupakan target minimal yang harus dicapai.

translated_text:
Article 11
(1) SPM as referred to in Article 9 paragraph (3) has performance indicators including:
a. coverage of Women and Children victims of violence who receive complaint handling by trained officers within the UPTD PPA;
b. coverage of Women and Children victims of violence who receive health services by trained health workers at Puskesmas and at Hospitals;
c. coverage of social rehabilitation services provided by trained social rehabilitation officers for Women and Children victims of violence within the UPTD PPA;
d. coverage of spiritual guidance services provided by trained spiritual guidance officers for Women and Children victims of violence within the UPTD PPA;
e. coverage of legal aid services for women and children victims of violence;
f. coverage of recovery services/psychological services for women and children victims of violence;
g. coverage of mediation services for women and children victims of violence;
h. coverage of repatriation services for women and children victims of violence; and
i. coverage of social reintegration services for women and children victims of violence.
(2) The determination of SPM UPTD PPA performance indicators for Women and Children victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) constitutes the minimum target that must be achieved.

text:
BAB IX
PEMBINAAN DAN PENGAWASAN
Pasal 14
(1) Bupati melakukan pembinaan dan pengawasan penyelenggaraan UPTD PPA. (2) Pembinaan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi:
a. pedoman dan standar pemenuhan;
b. bimbingan teknis dan pelatihan;
c. supervisi;
d. penyediaan fasilitas;
e. monitoring; dan
f. evaluasi.
(3) Pembinaan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) dalam rangka mewujudkan  tujuan perlindungan perempuan dan Anak korban kekerasan sesuai standar  pelayanan minimal.

translated_text:
CHAPTER IX
GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION
Article 14
(1) The Regent conducts guidance and supervision of the implementation of UPTD PPA. (2) Guidance as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:
a. guidelines and fulfillment standards;
b. technical guidance and training;
c. supervision;
d. provision of facilities;
e. monitoring; and
f. evaluation.
(3) Guidance as referred to in paragraph (2) is in order to realize the objectives of protection for women and children victims of violence in accordance with minimum service standards.
